'''Sacrifice of Blood''' is a [[keystone passive skill]]/[[keyword]] which causes [[life regeneration]] while at [[full life]] to give the user a Blood Barrier that can absorb damage from incoming [[hit]]s, at the cost of halving the user's life regeneration rate.

Sacrifice of Blood can only be obtained via {{psl|Corruption's Embrace}} from the [[Chaos Bloodline]].

==Mechanics==
Sacrifice of Blood will only grant a Blood Barrier while the conditions for [[full life]] is active. Any life [[reservation]] or mechanics preventing life from recovering to full such as {{il|Petrified Blood}} will block it. The {{c|mod|You count as on Full Life while at 90% of maximum Life or above}} [[Life Mastery]] will grant Blood Barrier while you have at least 90% life, and {{il|Coward's Chains}} will cause you to always gain Blood Barrier. 

Blood Barrier is granted based on tooltip life regeneration including modifiers to life regeneration rate; modifiers to life recovery rate does not affect Blood Barrier gain. The actual life recovered per second is not considered and the rate of gain is not affected by any ongoing [[damage over time]] or life loss over time effects (as long as you're on full life). This allows Sacrifice of Blood to be used with effects that prevent recovery from life regeneration like {{psl|Vaal Pact}}.

It cannot be used with {{psl|Zealot's Oath}} since all life regeneration gets converted.  It is also incompatible with stats that grant {{c|mod|Life Recovery from Regeneration is not applied}}, such as {{il|Kaom's Spirit}} and the {{c|mod|Every 4 seconds, Recover 1 Life for every 0.1 Life Recovery per second from Regeneration}} [[Recovery Mastery]].

Blood Barrier absorbs damage from hits after it is absorbed by [[aegis]] effects or [[guard skill]]s, but before [[ward]].

